cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Implementation of the BFSC plate finite element in 2D
type: software
abstract: >-
  The `bfscplate2d` module implements the BFSC plate finite element in 2D,
  a four-node rectangular element of the classical laminated plate theory,
  with the nonlinear strains of von Karman, aiming linear and nonlinear
  analyses. It computes the contributions of each element to:

  * The linear constitutive stiffness matrix, for linear static analyses

  * The geometric stiffness matrix, for linear buckling analyses

  * The mass matrix, for natural frequency analyses

  * The internal force vector and the tangent stiffness matrix, for
    geometrically nonlinear static analyses
message: >-
  Please, cite this software using:
  Saullo G. P. Castro (2026). Implementation of the BFSC plate finite element in 2D (Version 0.4.1). https://github.com/saullocastro/bfscplate2d.
